  "query_preview": "..\nAs a newly-formed tropical disturbance Invest 97W (which replaced \nformer Invest 95W) continues to move away from the region to the\nnorthwest, the enhanced monsoon surge that was expected to develop\nacross the Marianas is not likely to return anytime soon. As such,\nintense rainfall and significant gusty winds are no longer expected\nat this time, so the Special Weather Statement was allowed to expire.\nHowever, a generally moderate southwesterly monsoon pattern will \ncontinue to bring patchy showers and some thunderstorms through \nFriday night, followed by a momentary resurgence in convection at a \nleading edge of the monsoon trough and embedded col that may bring \nnumerous and potentially heavy showers Saturday and Saturday night. \nConditions will then improve considerably thereafter, with a dry \nspell to ensue around Labor Day.",
